<div class="wrap page-head"><p class="kicker">A sister imprint of the Foundation</p><h1>Eastern Christian Publications</h1><p class="lede">A publishing house in Fairfax, Virginia, specializing in books on the Eastern Christian Churches, Catholic and Orthodox, and a forum for ecumenical dialogue through the Eastern Churches Journal.</p></div>
<section class="band" style="padding-top:1.5rem">
  <div class="wrap two-col top">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="dropcap">Eastern Christian Publications grew up alongside the conferences. It publishes the proceedings of every Orientale Lumen gathering, the Lectures from Rome series, adult catechesis, liturgical theology, historical reprints, and the writings of Metropolitan Kallistos, Robert Taft, Robert Slesinski, Jack Custer, and Jack Figel among others.</p>
      <p>Its best-known work is the Byzantine Daily Office, an English Book of Hours in the Ruthenian recension for parish and personal prayer, and the EC Bulletin Service, which produces weekly bulletins for Eastern Catholic parishes.</p>
      <p>The catalog is online, with ordering by card or by check to the Fairfax office. Contract publishing is available for parishes, eparchies, and authors.</p>
